{
  "schema": "configuration-comparison-conformance/v1",
  "note": "The shared conformance fixture for compareConfigurations (issue #1254, configuration-comparison/v1). Each case gives one synthetic `input` and one to four `sides`: the runtime-config/v1 data members as `config`, the exact `ruleset` text and a per-side `actionPolicy` document. `expect` is a projection: per side the `status`, the `failure` code and the findings as type, detector and range in Unicode code points, and per side the `differences` against side 0 (null when none is reported). The Rust core and every JavaScript surface that loads a binding run every case for each listed profile and compare the same projection. Expected values are authored here; no surface derives them. No case carries a real credential.",
